    "comments": {
      "/": {
        "comment_0": "Sensing reset is problematic as the edge cannot be detected (as it would reset the design). Only state of reset can be confirmed!\nThe sys_clock is samples at 400 MHz while the clock itself runs at 100MHz. We should see 4 ticks per 100 Mhz cycle (which is true)",
        "comment_2": "Must use a clock wizard on sys_clock",
        "comment_3": "May need to move SDRAM to its own SMC in the future",
        "comment_4": "MIG7 Sys clock must be connected to 100 MHz clock directly for low jitter "
      }
    },
